      "writtenOn": "2023-01-12T08:35:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I would suggest rewording this part since this is also the first paragraph and the reader may not have a lot of context. It\u0027s a bit sudden to jump directly into how trimming work without explaining why trimming is needed.\n\nHere are some ideas: One key aspect is that, to avoid data loss, it is necessary to keep a copy of the server-provided proto, including unknown fields and partially-supported fields (e.g. partially-implemented functionality or functionality guarded behind a feature toggle). Storing a fully copy of a proto may have performance impact (memory, disk), the Sync infrastructure allows and encourages features to trim proto fields that do not need an additional copy, if the field is already well supported by the client.",
      "revId": "febe122f8553364223dd0568be3eca0c5b909e1d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
